uot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:true,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://erinmindfulmoments.substack.com/i/218589358?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5ef48864-0b6e-4c51-baf0-db4059c008b5_1672x941.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!xRuw!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5ef48864-0b6e-4c51-baf0-db4059c008b5_1672x941.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!xRuw!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5ef48864-0b6e-4c51-baf0-db4059c008b5_1672x941.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!xRuw!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5ef48864-0b6e-4c51-baf0-db4059c008b5_1672x941.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!xRuw!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5ef48864-0b6e-4c51-baf0-db4059c008b5_1672x941.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" fetchpriority=\"high\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>Wellbeing may feel personal, yet it shapes our shared lives. This was the key theme of the latest <a href=\"https://insighttimer.com/erinmindfulmoments/events\">Take A Pause Live</a> session.</p><p>We turned to the <a href=\"https://www.dhammatalks.org/suttas/SN/SN47_19.html\">Sedaka Sutta (SN 47.19)</a>, which describes a metaphor of two acrobats balancing on a bamboo pole. <em>Each acrobat must attend to their own balance for both of them to be safe.</em> </p><p>The teaching goes further: <em><strong>cultivating mindfulness protects both ourselves and others</strong></em>. </p><p>When we tend to our own mind and body, we are at the same time taking care of our relationship with others. </p><p>And when we choose to meet others with patience, harmlessness, goodwill, and sympathy, these qualities, in turn, help steady us.</p><p>Imagine a tense morning at home or a difficult conversation at work. When we pause to notice a tight jaw, tiredness, or a flash of impatience, we gain a moment to choose our response more wisely. This pause is what keeps a hurtful remark or unwholesome behaviour from landing on someone else. </p><p>And when we listen with attentiveness and compassion to a person who is struggling, the sense of balance, steadiness and ease we are cultivating within will protect us.</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!v9rP!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F10197714-1032-46a2-85e6-f84cd84f443e_1672x940.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!v9rP!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F10197714-1032-46a2-85e6-f84cd84f443e_1672x940.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!v9rP!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F10197714-1032-46a2-85e6-f84cd84f443e_1672x940.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!v9rP!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F10197714-1032-46a2-85e6-f84cd84f443e_1672x940.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!v9rP!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F10197714-1032-46a2-85e6-f84cd84f443e_1672x940.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!v9rP!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F10197714-1032-46a2-85e6-f84cd84f443e_1672x940.png\" width=\"1456\" height=\"819\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/10197714-1032-46a2-85e6-f84cd84f443e_1672x940.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:819,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:3112024,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://erinmindfulmoments.substack.com/i/218589358?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F10197714-1032-46a2-85e6-f84cd84f443e_1672x940.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!v9rP!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F10197714-1032-46a2-85e6-f84cd84f443e_1672x940.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!v9rP!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F10197714-1032-46a2-85e6-f84cd84f443e_1672x940.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!v9rP!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F10197714-1032-46a2-85e6-f84cd84f443e_1672x940.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!v9rP!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F10197714-1032-46a2-85e6-f84cd84f443e_1672x940.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>In our meditation, we were invited to begin with the body: <em>watch what is present, notice any worry or fatigue, and resist the urge to judge or fix it</em>. </p><p>We were reminded that no perfect calm was required, and that honest awareness and acceptance of each moment offered a useful place to start.</p><p>From there, we considered how an inner state might shape the next interaction with our experience. </p><p>We reflected on <em><strong>the nature of cause and effect</strong></em> — how a reaction to an inner state can translate into impulses and behaviours that impact our outer landscape. </p><p>Erin also introduced <em>mettā</em>, the practice of offering kind wishes to ourselves and others. </p><p>We might quietly wish for patience with our feelings and enough space to respond wisely. Then we can extend that wish to the people sharing our day.</p><p>A key takeaway from practising together: <strong>Our wellbeing is interconnected</strong>. Caring for ourselves gives us more room to care for others, and caring for others can strengthen the qualities that sustain our own peace of mind.</p><div><hr></div><h3><strong>Tap Play to Meditate:</strong></h3><div class=\"native-audio-embed\" data-component-name=\"AudioPlaceholder\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;label&quot;:null,&quot;mediaUploadId&quot;:&quot;cca8c4f7-398e-41cd-9008-cf46785be3e2&quot;,&quot;duration&quot;:1412.2057,&quot;downloadable&quot;:false,&quot;isEditorNode&quot;:true}\"></div><div class=\"captioned-button-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://erinmindfulmoments.substack.com/p/my-wellbeing-our-wellbeing?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Share&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CaptionedButtonToDOM\"><div class=\"preamble\"><p class=\"cta-caption\">This post is free for some time, and then archived for paid subscribers to support a sustainable, long-term sharing of mindful content. To support Erin’s work, upgrade to receive lifetime access to the full archive and ongoing updates.</p></div><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://erinmindfulmoments.substack.com/p/my-wellbeing-our-wellbeing?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Share&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://erinmindfulmoments.substack.com/p/my-wellbeing-our-wellbeing?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share\"><span>Share</span></a></p></div><div><hr></div><h3>Join Erin at Take A Pause Live </h3><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!cF0k!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff037c388-86a0-493a-80be-03afaf174024_1100x761.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!cF0k!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff037c388-86a0-493a-80be-03afaf174024_1100x761.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!cF0k!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff037c388-86a0-493a-80be-03afaf174024_1100x761.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!cF0k!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff037c388-86a0-493a-80be-03afaf174024_1100x761.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!cF0k!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff037c388-86a0-493a-80be-03afaf174024_1100x761.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!cF0k!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff037c388-86a0-493a-80be-03afaf174024_1100x761.png\" width=\"1100\" height=\"761\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/f037c388-86a0-493a-80be-03afaf174024_1100x761.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:761,&quot;width&quot;:1100,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:null,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;Take A Pause Live community on Insight Timer with Erin Lee&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:null,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"Take A Pause Live community on Insight Timer with Erin Lee\" title=\"Take A Pause Live community on Insight Timer with Erin Lee\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!cF0k!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff037c388-86a0-493a-80be-03afaf174024_1100x761.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!cF0k!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff037c388-86a0-493a-80be-03afaf174024_1100x761.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!cF0k!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff037c388-86a0-493a-80be-03afaf174024_1100x761.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!cF0k!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff037c388-86a0-493a-80be-03afaf174024_1100x761.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><blockquote><p><strong>Saturdays 7:30 AM Singapore Time</strong></p><p><strong>Sundays 9:00 PM Singapore Time</strong></p></blockquote><p>Sometimes all we need is a pause, to understand how to live better. </p><p>Initiated by Mindfulness Coach Erin Lee, we keep the spirit of Take A Pause intentionally simple: gathering at the end of each week, paying attention together, sharing a short reading, and reflecting on a key teaching to carry into the days ahead.​ </p><p>We are a community not because of structure or formality, but because we show up—for ourselves and for one another—and become quiet accountability partners on this path of mindful living. </p><p>All are welcome to join!</p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://insighttimer.com/erinmindfulmoments/events&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Join Take A Pause Live&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://insighttimer.com/erinmindfulmoments/events\"><span>Join Take A Pause Live</span></a></p><p></p>",
  "body_text": "Wellbeing may feel personal, yet it shapes our shared lives. This was the key theme of the latest Take A Pause Live session.\n\nWe turned to the Sedaka Sutta (SN 47.19), which describes a metaphor of two acrobats balancing on a bamboo pole. Each acrobat must attend to their own balance for both of them to be safe. \n\nThe teaching goes further: cultivating mindfulness protects both ourselves and others. \n\nWhen we tend to our own mind and body, we are at the same time taking care of our relationship with others. \n\nAnd when we choose to meet others with patience, harmlessness, goodwill, and sympathy, these qualities, in turn, help steady us.\n\nImagine a tense morning at home or a difficult conversation at work. When we pause to notice a tight jaw, tiredness, or a flash of impatience, we gain a moment to choose our response more wisely. This pause is what keeps a hurtful remark or unwholesome behaviour from landing on someone else. \n\nAnd when we listen with attentiveness and compassion to a person who is struggling, the sense of balance, steadiness and ease we are cultivating within will protect us.\n\nIn our meditation, we were invited to begin with the body: watch what is present, notice any worry or fatigue, and resist the urge to judge or fix it. \n\nWe were reminded that no perfect calm was required, and that honest awareness and acceptance of each moment offered a useful place to start.\n\nFrom there, we considered how an inner state might shape the next interaction with our experience. \n\nWe reflected on the nature of cause and effect — how a reaction to an inner state can translate into impulses and behaviours that impact our outer landscape. \n\nErin also introduced mettā, the practice of offering kind wishes to ourselves and others. \n\nWe might quietly wish for patience with our feelings and enough space to respond wisely. Then we can extend that wish to the people sharing our day.\n\nA key takeaway from practising together: Our wellbeing is interconnected. Caring for ourselves gives us more room to care for others, and caring for others can strengthen the qualities that sustain our own peace of mind.\n\n---\n\nTap Play to Meditate:\n\nThis post is free for some time, and then archived for paid subscribers to support a sustainable, long-term sharing of mindful content. To support Erin’s work, upgrade to receive lifetime access to the full archive and ongoing updates.\n\nShare\n\n---\n\nJoin Erin at Take A Pause Live \n\nSaturdays 7:30 AM Singapore Time\n\nSundays 9:00 PM Singapore Time\n\nSometimes all we need is a pause, to understand how to live better. \n\nInitiated by Mindfulness Coach Erin Lee, we keep the spirit of Take A Pause intentionally simple: gathering at the end of each week, paying attention together, sharing a short reading, and reflecting on a key teaching to carry into the days ahead.​ \n\nWe are a community not because of structure or formality, but because we show up—for ourselves and for one another—and become quiet accountability partners on this path of mindful living. \n\nAll are welcome to join!\n\nJoin Take A Pause Live",
